From 8a095ae107e7576a804a9e396100f94d272ffa56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Close the post-session loop and add a resource library

Three additions, all riding the existing email rails (email_queue ->
email-dispatch every 15 min, enqueue_teaching_reminders daily at 9am ET):

1. Session report. The morning after a session the teacher gets an email
   asking them to confirm attendance, record the topics they discussed,
   and note learning gaps plus suggested future topics. The email links
   into My Teaching, where the report form folds the attendance roster in
   as step 1 so it is one save rather than two. Filing marks the session
   delivered and emails the director a copy, so suggestions reach the
   person who plans the curriculum.

2. Fellow feedback request. The same morning, every active fellow is asked
   to rate the session and say what they would like taught next. Sent to
   the whole roster rather than only fellows marked present: attendance is
   often recorded late, and a request that silently never sends is worse
   than one an absent fellow ignores.

3. Library. A private storage bucket of reference PDFs. The director and
   program admin upload; anyone signed in downloads through signed URLs
   valid for an hour. Nothing is reachable from the public internet.

Also surfaces a Topic suggestions card on My Teaching for the director,
collecting what teachers and fellows have asked to see covered.

