From 4437566ff9aca6ab2d5106a20e3e0beb53397bab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Send post-session emails same day at 9:00 AM Toronto

The report and feedback requests were going out the morning after. They now
go out the same day at 09:00 local, which is exactly when the standard
08:00-09:00 session ends.

A fixed UTC cron cannot hold 9:00 AM local across daylight saving, so the
job becomes hourly and the function checks the Toronto clock itself,
returning immediately on the other 23 runs. That also fixes the pre-existing
drift where the 7-day and 1-day advance reminders arrived an hour early
every winter.

Sections 3 and 4 gain an end_time guard so a session scheduled later than
09:00 is never asked about before it has happened; it is picked up by the
next morning's run instead, bounded by a 7-day lookback. Existing sessions
before today are marked as already requested so that lookback cannot flood
inboxes on the first run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HV2TSLxfnBFbXmi2V2hHHf
---
