From d20a943170782fa4a80144cb84597894666ed254 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:35:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Treat a session as past once it ends, not at midnight

My Teaching split sessions on session_date >= today, so a session held this
morning stayed under "Upcoming" until midnight and every isPast-gated
control -- attendance, feedback, the session report, mark-delivered, the
completion letter -- was unreachable on the day it ran.

That was survivable when post-session emails went out the following
morning. Now that they go out at 9:00 AM the same day, the email sends the
teacher to a page with nothing on it.

sessionHasEnded() mirrors the end_time guard in
enqueue_teaching_reminders(), so the portal and the email agree on which
sessions are finished. My Teaching ticks once a minute so a page left open
across 09:00 flips over on its own.

Also replaces toISOString().slice(0, 10) with a local-timezone date. That
was the UTC date, which in Toronto rolls to tomorrow at 20:00 local -- a
session would have jumped to "Past" four hours early each evening.

Rate Teaching gets the same treatment: today's session is listed for rating
only once it has actually ended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HV2TSLxfnBFbXmi2V2hHHf
---
 src/lib/format.ts          | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/pages/MyTeaching.tsx   | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 src/pages/RateTeaching.tsx | 12 +++++++-----
 3 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/format.ts b/src/lib/format.ts
index ee4c3b2..5da73a7 100644
